{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527409111,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2NDgxNDE5NzQ="},"added":["windows"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527427044,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MjMzMDQ1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-392330452"},"message":"I forgot about that issue of limited max path length on Windows (due API restrictive) - is it no longer the case somehow? Ref: https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa365247(v=vs.85).aspx","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531506077,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNDkxMTUxNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-404911517"},"message":"I think I've ran into this one also while trying to `datalad install -r`  which was surprising since I did not use `-g` so I guess it should have not fetched anything but then it pukes on some .nii.gz key:\n![why](http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/gkrellShoot_07-13-18_140705.png)\nand the file is actually there\n![there](http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/gkrellShoot_07-13-18_140752.png)\n@joeyh any ideas?  I think I've also spotted at some point the webapp web frontend to appear -- is webapp running by default on windows somehow?","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531506077,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEwODA5MTIzNA=="},"target":"dbb0e505418691b7e172fdf18ae0d31343623f6533fb3701753affe29d6b97ce","message":"I think I've ran into this one also while trying to `datalad install -r`  which was surprising since I did not use `-g` so I guess it should have not fetched anything but then it pukes on some .nii.gz key:\n![why](http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/gkrellShoot_07-13-18_140705.png)\nand the file is actually there\n![there](http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/gkrellShoot_07-13-18_140752.png)\n@joeyh any ideas?  I think I've also spotted at some point the webapp web frontend to appear -- is webapp running by default on windows somehow?\n\nanother interesting aspect is that then `datalad get` seems to work just fine, and doing it manually with git clone/git annex init replicates it:\n![init fails](http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/gkrellShoot_07-13-18_142017.png)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531506292,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNDkxNDc5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-404914796"},"message":"@joeyh I guess git-annex tries to verify something but is running it under some other than the tree root directory in direct mode?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531507814,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNDkyMTE5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-404921195"},"message":"ah, this is a good old issue: http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/__34__git-annex__58___direct__58___1_failed__34___on_Windows/  . A resolution suggested was to enable long file names support.  In my case  I am on Windows 7 6.1.7601 ... not yet sure if long files support is possible on that beast","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1531508025,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNDkyMjExMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-404922110"},"message":"Yaroslav Halchenko wrote:\n\u003e I think I've ran into this one also while trying to datalad install -r which\n\u003e was surprising since I did not use -g so I guess it should have not fetched\n\u003e anything but then it pukes on some .nii.gz key:\n\u003e why\n\u003e and the file is actually there\n\u003e there\n\nWindows path limits are still very much an issue, and that is the\nfailure mode I've seen when the path is too long. It's traversing\nall annex links in the repository to enable direct mode.\n\nThe full path is something like \nC:\\\\Users\\\\DatLad\\\\datalad\\\\labs\\\\gobbini\\\\famface\\\\data\\.git\\annex\\objects\\db3\\781\\SHA256E-s684528--\\f43c828ffc1ad6cf854f8545f60c2d50f27ff3cfe8cabe2aa7a207cfb02b6f61281b.nii.gz\nwhich is around 177 characters.. git-annex uses relative paths where it can and it\nseems to have done so here, which is only 120 characters. The windows MAX_PATH is\nactually supposed to be 260 characters, so it's a bit surprising it fails on that.\n\nAlthough that path is to the object directory, the temp file within it would add\nmore length -- perhaps openTempFile is reporting the name of the directory it's\nmaking the temp file in and not the full temp file path. It might also\nbe making the path absolute internally.\n\nRunning Linux git-annex in WSL is a good way to avoid all this horribleness,\nit works pretty well except for one recent reversion in WSL that makes\nsqlite crash.\n\n\u003e @joeyh any ideas? I think I've also spotted at some point the webapp web\n\u003e frontend to appear -- is webapp running by default on windows somehow?\n\nThere's a git-annex-autostart.vbs that gets linked to\n\"$SMSTARTUP/git-annex-autostart.lnk\", but it runs git annex assistant\n--autostart; while that will start the webapp if you've configured\ngit-annex to autostart in some repository, it will not open a web\nbrowser on the webapp. (Aside from the nonsense of a visual basic script\nthat opens a hidden DOS box, this is identical to the Linux desktop\nautostart that git-annex installs.)\n\nThere's a git-annex-webapp.vbs that gets linked to\n\"$SMPROGRAMS/Git Annex (Webapp).lnk\" to put it on the Start menu\nto open the web browser.\n\nNot being a MS certified engineer, I can't comment as to what Windows\nmight do with items on the Start menu, as far as deciding to start them\nwithout you clicking on them.. Noone has ever complained to me about\nthat happening.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531511101,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNDkzNDc0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-404934749"},"message":"Thank you @joeyh for the details! -- FWIW I've tried on another repo (openfmri/ds0000001) where we used MD5E backend, so key names were shorter and everything seemed to work out nicely (could install/get/drop without problem), so indeed I guess I've ran into that path length issue.  I guess may be on this system the limit is even shorter.\nFWIW -- added a check to `datalad wtf` to try creating files of growing length... got up to 259 successfully in that directory so that system is nohow special ;-)  Moreover I did in IPython right there -- was able to open a file under there for writing following that path:\n![img](http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/gkrellShoot_07-13-18_154244.png)\nso it might be then haskell specific or something else...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531935675,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNjAxNTI3Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-406015277"},"message":"uff... so it is likely to be indeed just running into the limit of the max path length:\n```\nIn [1]: len(r'C:\\Users\\DataLad\\datalad\\labs\\gobbini\\famface\\data\\.git\\annex\\objec\n   ...: ts\\db3\\781\\SHA256E-s6845828--f4ec828ffc1ad6cf8545f60c2d50f27ff3cfe8cabe2a\n   ...: a7a207cfb02b6f61281b.nii.gz\\SHA256E-s6845828--f4ec828ffc1ad6cf8545f60c2d5\n   ...: 0f27ff3cfe8cabe2aa7a207cfb02b6f61281b.nii.gz')\nOut[1]: 257\n```\nWhen I moved that repo up under `c:\\tmp` `git annex init` finished correctly...\n\nlonger story: couldn't \"let it be\", so installed this niceish app for windows: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/procmon  and monitored execution when ran `git annex init` in that case where openTempFile fails.  Here is grepped for the SHA256E in csv export: http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/Logfile-1.CSV-781SHA256.txt and with +-5 lines around: http://www.onerussian.com/tmp/Logfile-1.CSV-781SHA256+5.txt .  So if we ever to debug calls etc on windows -- seems to be a nice tool! (didn't manage to get anywhere with windbg).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531935722,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNjAxNTUzMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2571#issuecomment-406015531"},"message":"since I think it is nothing more which could be fixed/accomplished for that , closing","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531935722,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTc0MDczOTA1NA=="},"status":2}]}